442217 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442217 1077 "selection" 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442217 1078 #edb/ref 17592186442212 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442217 1079 #uuid "d6d03c68-c527-56d7-8eec-20b909744859" 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442218 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442217 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442218 1069 "q-163159" 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442218 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442218 1071 "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}} \\\\ {e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at  $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ ∗\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 \\\\ 1 & ∗\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442218 1072 #uuid "afc538b7-6818-5bf5-a45c-82af4af91e85" 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442218 1074 "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}})=2{x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}})={e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}})={e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}})=-2{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}} & {e}^{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}} \\\\ {e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}} & -2{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n1+2+2=5.\n$$" 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442219 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442223 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442219 1062 #uuid "1cc56c04-dae4-5804-9f0a-0ad43a3a6deb" 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186442219 1063 #edb/ref 17592186367783 13194139534875 17592186045417 true] [17592186